  "pli-tv-bi-vb-ss2:1.11": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Jānāhi</i>, literally, “You know.” The implied meaning is not clear. However, in commenting on a different passage, one of the sub-commentaries, Sp-ṭ 4.330, defines the word as follows: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Jānāhīti cettha paṭipajjāti attho veditabbo</i>, “<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Jānāhi</i>: and here the meaning ‘undertake’ should be understood.” ",
